<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92043" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥάβδουχ-ος</span></b>  (properisp.), ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who carries a
				rod</i> or <i>staff of office</i>: </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>judge, umpire at a contest</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				338a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>magistrate's attendant, staff-bearer, beadle</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				734
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>UPZ</u>
				3.6
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>, prob.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				9(2).735
			</span></i> (Larissa, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				1109.24
			</span></i> (Coropa, <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Act.Ap.</u>
				16.35
			</span></i>; so, prob., in <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				5.50
			</span></i>: esp. at Rome, of the <i>lictors who carried the
			fasces</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				5.26.10
			</span></i>, etc.: also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥαβδοῦχοι, αἱ</span>, <i>female attendants</i>
			on Oenanthe, mother of Agathocles, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				15.29.13
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
